# Browser caches / profiles chromedp may spawn under the working dir, plus any
# built dossierx binary or throwaway project a test writes. The test harness
# already uses os.MkdirTemp / t.TempDir for its own scratch, but ignore these
# defensively so a stray artifact never gets committed.
dossierx
*.test
.chromedp/
chrome-user-data/
chromedp-*/
/tmp/

# site-text.json is the site extraction's OUTPUT (site_dom_test.go): every
# string a visitor can reach on either entry point, derived from a build of
# site/ at test time. It is evidence for one gate run, not a tracked artifact —
# unlike surface.json it cannot be byte-stable across machines, since producing
# it means running npm and a real browser.
site-text.json
